.\" Adapted from kbd 2.10.0 docs/man/man1/setleds.1, GPL-2.0-or-later.
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt SETLEDS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm setleds
.Nd report or change console keyboard locks and LEDs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl D | F | L
.Op Cm +num | -num
.Op Cm +caps | -caps
.Op Cm +scroll | -scroll
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
operates on the console connected to standard input.
With no operands it prints Num Lock, Caps Lock and Scroll Lock settings.
A plus operand sets its flag; a minus operand clears it.
Other flags stay unchanged.
.Pp
.Fl F ,
the default, changes the console's lock flags.
.Fl D
changes those flags and their defaults.
.Fl L
changes only the physical LEDs, independently of the lock flags;
.Fl L
alone restores LEDs that follow the lock flags.
.Fl v
reports the settings before and after a change.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
setleds -D +num < /dev/console
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loadkeys 1 ,
.Xr vconsole.conf 5
